<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Esat Digifone names Maloney as chief executive.</title>
<headline>Esat Digifone names Maloney as chief executive.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Esat Digifone had appointed Barry Maloney as chief executive with effect from July 1.</p>
<p>Maloney had been joint chief executive with Knut Digerud who is leaving the company to establish Telenor Ireland Ltd, grouping the Norwegian state telecom company's interests in Ireland under one umbrella.</p>
<p>Esat Digifone, which is 40 percent owned by Telenor and 40 percent by Esat Telecom, holds Ireland's second mobile phone licence.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
